---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import { sitePath } from '../lib/siteUrl';
import ClosingCTA from '../components/ClosingCTA.astro';
---

<Layout title="What is Varve?" description="Varve is a local-first design suite for vector, layout, typography, motion, prototyping, and print production — all in one cross-platform environment.">
  <div class="container-custom">
    <div class="product-page">
      <h1 class="page-hero-title">What is Varve?</h1>
      <p class="page-hero-sub">
        A local-first design suite for vector, layout, typography, motion, and print — one application, no account, no subscription, native on Linux. It runs natively on Linux, macOS, and Windows with a shared Rust engine. The desktop app writes projects to local files; there is no hosted web app yet.
      </p>

      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Connected creative workflows</h2>
        <p>
          Most creative work spans multiple disciplines. A poster needs vector shapes, typography, and print-ready export. A social media campaign needs layout, animation, and multiple output formats. A product design needs components, prototyping, and developer handoff.
        </p>
        <p>
          Varve is designed to keep this work in one place. Instead of switching between separate applications and rebuilding your context each time, you move between tasks within the same document, the same layer system, and the same interface.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Local-first, your files, your machine</h2>
        <p>
          Varve stores design data locally. No account or mandatory cloud sync is required, and core editing works offline. Optional model downloads, online font/icon search, user-configured providers, update checks, and aggregate measurements are separate network features; consented measurements do not include design content. You own your files, you control where they live, and the desktop application uses a native Rust engine. The same engine is compiled to WASM for the web target (a hosted web app is not available yet).
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Cross-platform native performance</h2>
        <p>
          Varve runs natively on Linux (CachyOS, Arch, Ubuntu, Fedora), macOS (Apple Silicon), and Windows (x86_64). The rendering architecture separates scene computation from display, using an intermediate representation that replays efficiently to the canvas. The same codebase powers both the native desktop and WASM web builds.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Source-available, shaped by its users</h2>
        <p>
          Varve is licensed under FSL-1.1-MIT — free to use, with source code available on GitHub. Development is transparent: architecture decisions, known limitations, and progress are documented publicly. Community input influences priorities. No VC pressure and no feature-checklist deadlines — features are built when they work, not when they sound good in marketing copy.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Who is Varve for?</h2>
        <div class="audience-grid">
          <div class="audience-card audience-card-terracotta">
            <span class="audience-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="13" rx="1.5"></rect>
                <path d="m7 8 3 3-3 3"></path>
                <path d="M12 14h5"></path>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3>Linux users</h3>
            <p>Creators on Linux who need a native design application with first-class platform support, CMYK print, and a Rust rendering engine.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="audience-card audience-card-teal">
            <span class="audience-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M12 3 3 8l9 5 9-5-9-5Z"></path>
                <path d="M3 16l9 5 9-5"></path>
                <path d="M3 12l9 5 9-5"></path>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3>Multi-disciplinary creators</h3>
            <p>Designers who switch between vector, layout, motion, and print work and want one document model instead of separate apps.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="audience-card audience-card-sandstone">
            <span class="audience-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="m3 21 6.5-1.5L20 9a2.1 2.1 0 0 0-3-3L6.5 16.5 5 21Z"></path>
                <path d="m15 5 4 4"></path>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3>Privacy-conscious creators</h3>
            <p>Freelancers and independents who want professional tools without subscription costs, cloud dependencies, or mandatory accounts.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="audience-card audience-card-ink">
            <span class="audience-icon" aria-hidden="true">
              <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.6" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round">
                <path d="M12 2 2 7l10 5 10-5-10-5Z"></path>
                <path d="M2 17l10 5 10-5"></path>
                <path d="M2 12l10 5 10-5"></path>
                <circle cx="12" cy="7" r="1.4" fill="currentColor" stroke="none"></circle>
              </svg>
            </span>
            <h3>Early adopters</h3>
            <p>People who want to test emerging workflows, report problems, and influence the direction of a developing creative tool.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Who Varve is not for (yet)</h2>
        <p>
          Because Varve is in beta, it is not yet the right choice for every situation:
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Critical production deadlines:</strong> expect bugs, incomplete tools, and workflow changes. Keep backups and test before relying on it for paid work.</li>
          <li><strong>Teams needing real-time collaboration:</strong> collaboration is not implemented — this is a single-user tool today.</li>
          <li><strong>Complex-script text:</strong> the engine has a canonical UAX #9 + paragraph layout pipeline (itemization, line breaking, visual run order, caret geometry), but live Canvas2D shaping and export parity for Arabic, Hebrew, Devanagari, Thai, and similar scripts remains in development.</li>
          <li><strong>Linux or Windows on ARM:</strong> only x86_64 is supported on those platforms (macOS builds target Apple Silicon).</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Coming from another design tool?</h2>
        <p>
          See <a href={sitePath('/compare')}>how Varve compares</a> to Figma, Adobe Illustrator,
          Affinity, Sketch, Inkscape, and Penpot &mdash; what's genuinely different, and where
          Varve still falls short today.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="product-section">
        <h2>Beta status</h2>
        <p>
          Varve is in public beta. Core features are functional and tested, but you may encounter bugs, incomplete tools, or changes to workflows and file formats as development continues. We recommend keeping backups of important work and not relying on Varve as the sole tool for critical production projects at this stage.
        </p>
        <p>
          The value of participating now: test emerging workflows, report problems that matter to you, and help shape where Varve goes next. See the <a href={sitePath('/support/known-issues')}>known issues</a> and <a href={sitePath('/releases')}>release notes</a> for current limitations.
        </p>
      </section>

  <ClosingCTA
    title="Try Varve"
    accentWord="beta."
    text="Free and source-available under FSL-1.1-MIT. Expect rough edges — it is an early release."
  />
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .product-page {
    max-width: 800px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 3rem 0 0;
  }
  
  .product-page .page-hero-title {
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .product-page .page-hero-sub {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  
  .product-section {
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
  }
  
  .product-section h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  
  .product-section p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.8;
  }

  .product-section ul {
    list-style: none;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .product-section li {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin-bottom: 0.6rem;
    padding-left: 1.5rem;
    position: relative;
  }

  .product-section li::before {
    content: "•";
    position: absolute;
    left: 0;
    color: var(--text-link-hover);
  }
  
  .audience-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 1.5rem;
    margin-top: 1.5rem;
  }
  
  .audience-card {
    position: relative;
    background: var(--surface-card);
    border: 1px solid var(--border-default);
    border-radius: 0.75rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    transition:
      transform var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default),
      border-color var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default),
      box-shadow var(--duration-fast) var(--ease-default);
  }

  @media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
    .audience-card:hover {
      transform: translateY(-2px);
      border-color: var(--border-strong);
      box-shadow: var(--elevation-shadow-raised);
    }
  }

  /* Icon badge: a small coloured tile above the title, one brand colour per
     card in rotation (teal/sandstone/terracotta/ink) — the same palette the
     logo strata use, so the grid reads as branded rather than decorated. */
  .audience-icon {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    width: 2.25rem;
    height: 2.25rem;
    border-radius: 0.625rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }

  .audience-card-teal .audience-icon {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--brand-teal) 18%, var(--surface-card));
    color: var(--brand-teal);
  }

  .audience-card-sandstone .audience-icon {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--brand-sandstone) 20%, var(--surface-card));
    color: var(--brand-sandstone);
  }

  .audience-card-terracotta .audience-icon {
    background: color-mix(in oklab, var(--brand-terracotta) 18%, var(--surface-card));
    color: var(--brand-terracotta);
  }

  .audience-card-ink .audience-icon {
    background: var(--surface-muted);
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }

  .audience-card h3 {
    font-size: 1.125rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--text-primary);
  }
  
  .audience-card p {
    color: var(--text-secondary);
    font-size: 0.9375rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  
  @media (max-width: 768px) {
    .product-page h1 {
      font-size: 2rem;
    }
    
    .product-intro {
      font-size: 1rem;
    }

    .audience-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
